[Music]  that's why  i love dirt roads is off granger smith's  tenth studio album aptly named  country things volume one it's the first  project from the texan native  who stepped away from the spotlight last  year after the tragic loss of his  three-year-old son  river now granger along with his wife  and their two other children are sharing  their emotional journey with their fans  in their youtube series called the  smiths and granger tells cheryl that as  difficult as it is for him to open up it  is  helping the family heal i want to thank  you for being so  open there are so many families who um  sadly have been in your position  what is the response been from fans and  even people who are  are new to your series we started the  channel  before our tragedy and so people  they took the journey with us in a lot  of ways we just wanted to  come on here and talk to you guys and  just let you know that we're seeing all  of your comments and we're getting all  of your letters  and we're receiving the outpouring of  love that you guys have given us these  past couple weeks and we just wanted to  say thank you  and kind of let you know how we're doing  it was difficult at times  i closed the smith channel down for  probably three months  and didn't do anything but then when i  opened it back up  it truly became a point of healing a a  vessel for us to to take out into  unknown waters and to  to show people what um what the next  step looks like what the next breath  looks like  i think the platform that we're that we  that we immediately stand  for is love those  close to you soak up those moments  you say hi everybody hi welcome to the  smiths  a lot of people have have gone through  maybe not something specifically like us  but some kind of loss knowing that if we  did that that would also help us  in our own process besides finding  solace  in their youtube series granger has also  turned to music  completing work on his album country  things volume one  you were in the process of writing and  creating this 10th studio album  and you stepped away as you said to to  mourn and to heal  what did you learn about yourself as a  as a person as a dad as an artist  during that time it was just really  focusing on  really honing in on the things that  matter  living in the present or being at least  being aware of the present moment that  tomorrow is not guaranteed  that we always get in this rat race of  especially the music business  the next album the next single the next  tour planning for the next  and less of concentrating on what we  have today  the blessing that today and the present  moment is to us  and i think that's what really happened  to me most is sharing your story  helped the healing process yeah it  really has um i would say probably more  so right now for my wife  she finds meaning and sharing  more openly about her feelings knowing  that  like you said there's people that could  then come forward and say  i i'm going through something similar  and now watching you do amber express  yourself  it's giving me hope

